<p>Disclaimer: The current state of this question does not really feel suitable for StackOverflow to me (the reproducer is way too large, see <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/help/minimal-reproducible-example">https://stackoverflow.com/help/minimal-reproducible-example</a> and this is now a &quot;please help debugging this&quot; question). I will go with it anyway.</p>
<p>What I did so far: I got the reproducing program in version 48c00ba73b311effa530c7372c89102fb70a18a6 and tried to find the right pieces of code. I am not sure whether I ended up looking at the correct code.</p>
<p>What I did find: Your program is drawing the red lines to the wrong window. And in a way so that they seem to stay after drawing. I figured that out by asking cairo do write out a PNG file of what was being drawn:</p>
